<div class="mb-8">
  <Heading size="2xl" as="h1" class="mb-2">Card</Heading>
  <Text size="lg" tone="subdued" as="h2">
    A structured container for grouping related content with optional header, body, and footer
    sections. Cards provide visual separation and hierarchy on a page.
  </Text>
</div>

<!-- Canonical example -->
<div class="mb-8">
  <Example source={'
    <Card>
      <Card:Header>
        <Header:Title>Card Title</Header:Title>
        <Header:Description>Card description</Header:Description>
      </Card:Header>

      <Text as="p">This is the card body with some example content.</Text>

      <Card:Footer>
        <Button>Action</Button>
      </Card:Footer>
    </Card>
  '}/>
</div>

<!-- Usage -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Usage</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <CodeBlock code={"<Card>\n  <Card:Header>\n    <Header:Title>Title</Header:Title>\n    <Header:Description>Description</Header:Description>\n  </Card:Header>\n  Content here\n  <Card:Footer>Footer content</Card:Footer>\n</Card>"}/>
  </div>
  <Prose class="mt-4">
    <p>
      Cards use a nested slot structure. All slots are optional — you can use just a body, or just a
      header and footer, depending on your needs.
    </p>
  </Prose>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-muted/50 overflow-hidden mt-4">
    <CodeBlock code={"Card\n├── Card:Header\n│   ├── Header:Title\n│   ├── Header:Description\n│   └── Header:Action\n├── content (direct)\n└── Card:Footer"}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- When to Use -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">When to Use</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Cards are the building blocks of dashboard layouts, settings pages, and any view where content
      naturally groups into distinct sections. They work well for profile summaries, form containers,
      feature highlights, and data panels.
    </p>
    <p>
      Avoid cards when the content is a single flat list or a continuous flow of text. In those cases
      the card border adds visual noise without providing meaningful grouping. Consider a simple
      divider or heading instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      For content that can be expanded or collapsed, consider an
      <a href="/components/accordion">Accordion</a>. For overlaid content that requires user
      interaction, use a <a href="/components/dialog">Dialog</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Behaviour -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Behaviour</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Cards are purely structural — they provide layout and visual grouping but carry no interactive
      behaviour by default. Each slot renders its content inside a styled <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>
      with appropriate padding and spacing.
    </p>
    <p>
      The header section lays out the title and description vertically, with an optional action slot
      that renders inline for contextual controls like an "Add" button or a dropdown menu.
    </p>
    <p>
      The footer typically holds action buttons. Use <code>flex justify-between</code> inside the
      footer to place a cancel button on the left and a submit button on the right.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Examples -->
<div class="flex flex-col gap-12 mb-12">
  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">With Action Button</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Use the <code>Header:Action</code> slot to place a contextual control alongside the title.
        This is useful for "Add", "Edit", or overflow menu buttons.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <Card>
        <Card:Header>
          <Header:Title>Team Members</Header:Title>
          <Header:Description>Manage your team and invite new members.</Header:Description>
          <Header:Action>
            <Button variant="outline" size="sm"><Icon name="plus" size="sm"/>Add</Button>
          </Header:Action>
        </Card:Header>

        <Text as="p">You currently have 5 team members across 2 projects.</Text>

        <Card:Footer>
          <Button variant="secondary">View all members</Button>
        </Card:Footer>
      </Card>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Form Card</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Cards are a natural container for forms. Place form fields in the body and submit/cancel
        buttons in the footer for a clean, consistent layout.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <Card>
        <Card:Header>
          <Header:Title>Create Project</Header:Title>
          <Header:Description>Fill in the details to start a new project.</Header:Description>
        </Card:Header>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <TextField label="Project Name" placeholder="Enter project name" fullwidth/>
          <TextField label="Description" placeholder="Brief description" multiline=3 fullwidth/>
        </div>

        <Card:Footer>
          <div class="flex justify-between w-full">
            <Button variant="ghost">Cancel</Button>
            <Button>Create</Button>
          </div>
        </Card:Footer>
      </Card>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Minimal Card</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>All slots are optional. A card with just a body is useful for simple content blocks that
        need visual separation from their surroundings.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <Card>

        <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
          <Icon name="circle-info" size="lg" class="text-blue-500"/>
          <Text as="p">Your trial expires in 7 days. Upgrade to keep your data.</Text>
        </div>

      </Card>
    '}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Best Practices -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Best Practices</Heading>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-green-500/30 bg-green-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-green-600">Do</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Use cards to group logically related content together.</li>
          <li>Keep titles short and descriptions informative.</li>
          <li>Place primary actions in the footer, contextual actions in the header.</li>
          <li>Use consistent card sizes within a grid layout.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-red-600">Don't</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Nest cards inside other cards — it creates confusing depth.</li>
          <li>Use cards for every piece of content; some content flows better without borders.</li>
          <li>Put too many actions in the footer — two or three is the maximum.</li>
          <li>Use cards as buttons; if the whole card should be clickable, wrap it in a link.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- API Reference -->
<div>
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">API Reference</Heading>

  <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 mt-6">Card</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Slot</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y">
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">Card:Header</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Optional header section containing title, description, and action.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">Card:Footer</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Bottom section, typically used for action buttons.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 mt-6">Card:Header</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Slot</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y">
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">Header:Title</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">The card's heading text.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">Header:Description</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Subtitle or supporting text below the title.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">Header:Action</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Inline control rendered alongside the title (button, dropdown, etc.).</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
